      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <limits.h>\n\nstatic void insert_candidate(float *distances, char *labels, int *indices,\n                             int k, float d, char label, int idx) {\n    for (int x = 0; x < k; ++x) {\n        if (distances[x] < 0.0f ||\n            d < distances[x] ||\n            (d == distances[x] && idx < indices[x])) {\n            for (int y = k - 1; y > x; --y) {\n                distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n                indices[y] = indices[y - 1];\n            }\n            distances[x] = d;\n            labels[x] = label;\n            indices[x] = idx;\n            return;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    int *offsets = (int *) malloc(sizeof(int) * (n_groups + 1));\n    offsets[0] = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; ++i) {\n        offsets[i + 1] = offsets[i] + groups[i].length;\n    }\n\n    float *global_distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n    char *global_labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    int *global_indices = (int *) malloc(sizeof(int) * k);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        global_distances[i] = -1.0f;\n        global_labels[i] = 0;\n        global_indices[i] = INT_MAX;\n    }\n\n#pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        float *local_distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n        char *local_labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n        int *local_indices = (int *) malloc(sizeof(int) * k);\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n            local_distances[i] = -1.0f;\n            local_labels[i] = 0;\n            local_indices[i] = INT_MAX;\n        }\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(guided)\n        for (int g = 0; g < n_groups; ++g) {\n            Group group = groups[g];\n            int base_index = offsets[g];\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < group.length; ++j) {\n                float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, group.points[j]);\n                insert_candidate(local_distances, local_labels, local_indices,\n                                 k, d, group.label, base_index + j);\n            }\n        }\n\n#pragma omp critical\n        {\n            for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n                if (local_distances[i] >= 0.0f) {\n                    insert_candidate(global_distances, global_labels, global_indices,\n                                     k, local_distances[i], local_labels[i],\n                                     local_indices[i]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        free(local_distances);\n        free(local_labels);\n        free(local_indices);\n    }\n\n    qsort(global_labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = global_labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; ++i) {\n        if (global_labels[i] != global_labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = global_labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            ++current_frequency;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = global_labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(offsets);\n    free(global_distances);\n    free(global_labels);\n    free(global_indices);\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Parallelize per-group distance and top-k selection with OpenMP guided work sharing. Each thread maintains a private top-k list keyed by (distance, original point index), preserving the sequential tie-breaking rule exactly; private lists are merged under one critical section after an implicit barrier.",
  "notes": "The implementation remains correct even if OpenMP is disabled because all pragmas are ignored and the single-thread path performs the same ordered insertion. The extra index field makes tie handling independent of scheduling order: for equal squared distances, the earliest input point wins as in the sequential baseline. Only src/knn.c was changed; knn.h is untouched.",
